# Scheduled-workflow staleness stamp (ADR-051 / P101). Written by
# `scripts/schedule-refresh.mjs`, read by the SessionStart reporter.
#
# ANCHORED RULE, so it carries the strip hazard recorded above: this pattern has
# a mid-pattern separator and is therefore anchored to the repo root. If a move
# strips it, the stamp gets committed and every clone reads someone else's
# machine's success timestamp -- so the reporter prints nothing and a stale
# schedule goes unreported. A silent green produced by an ignore-rule strip,
# which is the composite this file has already met twice.
# `schedule-hook-wiring.test.mjs` asserts BOTH that the rule matches and that
# the path is untracked, because check-ignore proves the rule and says nothing
# about a path that was tracked before the rule landed.
.addressr-state/
